@startuml
' diagrams/p2p-payment-flow.puml
' Diagram 1 of 4: HAPPY PATH
title P2P Payment — Happy Path

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Transaction\nOrchestrator" as ORCH
participant "Redis\n(idempotency)" as REDIS
participant "Payment\nProcessing Svc" as PAY
participant "Fraud\nDetection Svc" as FRAUD
participant "Account Svc\n(Shard A - sender)" as ACC_A
participant "Account Svc\n(Shard B - receiver)" as ACC_B
database "PostgreSQL\n(Citus)" as DB
queue "Kafka" as KAFKA

Client -> GW: POST /payments\n(Idempotency-Key: K1)
GW -> ORCH: forward request
ORCH -> REDIS: GET idempotency:K1
REDIS --> ORCH: not found
ORCH -> DB: INSERT transaction\n(status=INITIATED, saga_id)
ORCH -> REDIS: SET idempotency:K1 = IN_PROGRESS (TTL 24h)

ORCH -> PAY: process(txn)
PAY -> FRAUD: evaluate(txn)\n[sync, 15ms SLA]
FRAUD --> PAY: APPROVED

PAY -> ACC_A: debit(account_A, amount, expected_version=v)
ACC_A -> DB: UPDATE accounts SET available_balance -= amount,\nversion = v+1 WHERE account_id=A AND version=v
DB --> ACC_A: 1 row updated
ACC_A --> PAY: debited (new_version=v+1)

PAY -> ACC_B: credit(account_B, amount, expected_version=w)
ACC_B -> DB: UPDATE accounts SET available_balance += amount,\nversion = w+1 WHERE account_id=B AND version=w
DB --> ACC_B: 1 row updated
ACC_B --> PAY: credited (new_version=w+1)

PAY --> ORCH: saga steps complete
ORCH -> DB: INSERT ledger_entries (debit leg, credit leg)\nUPDATE transaction SET status=COMPLETED
ORCH -> KAFKA: outbox: txn.completed
ORCH -> REDIS: SET idempotency:K1 = COMPLETED (result cached)
ORCH --> GW: 200 OK {transaction_id, status: COMPLETED}
GW --> Client: 200 OK

== async, off critical path ==
KAFKA -->> "Notification Svc": txn.completed
KAFKA -->> "Audit Svc": txn.completed
KAFKA -->> "Reconciliation Svc": txn.completed

@enduml

@startuml
' Diagram 2 of 4: FAILURE SCENARIO 1 — Sender shard down mid-transaction (ARB Q2)
title P2P Payment — Failure Scenario 1: Sender's DB Shard Down Mid-Transaction

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Transaction\nOrchestrator" as ORCH
participant "Payment\nProcessing Svc" as PAY
participant "Account Svc\n(Shard A - sender)" as ACC_A
database "DB Shard A\n(PRIMARY DOWN)" as DBA #FFCCCC
database "DB Shard A\n(REPLICA)" as DBA_R
queue "Kafka" as KAFKA

Client -> GW: POST /payments
GW -> ORCH: forward
ORCH -> PAY: process(txn)
PAY -> ACC_A: debit(account_A, amount, expected_version=v)
ACC_A -> DBA: UPDATE accounts ... WHERE account_id=A
DBA --> ACC_A: **connection timeout**\n(2 failures / 5s threshold)

note over ACC_A #FFCCCC
  **Detecting component: CB-DB-PRIMARY**
  (circuit breaker on Account Service's
  DB connection pool)
  Trips after threshold met.
  Fallback per reference table:
  "Route reads to replica; queue writes"
end note

ACC_A -> ACC_A: CB-DB-PRIMARY OPENS
ACC_A --> PAY: ERROR: SHARD_UNAVAILABLE\n(debit never committed)

note over PAY, ORCH
  **Compensation logic: NONE REQUIRED.**
  The debit UPDATE never committed (no row
  was modified — connection failed before
  transaction commit). There is nothing to
  roll back. This is the key correctness
  property: partial commits cannot occur
  because the failure happened pre-commit.
end note

PAY --> ORCH: step failed, no compensation needed
ORCH -> ORCH: UPDATE transaction SET status=FAILED,\nfailure_reason=SHARD_UNAVAILABLE
ORCH -> KAFKA: outbox: txn.failed
ORCH --> GW: 503 {status: FAILED,\nreason: "shard temporarily unavailable"}
GW --> Client: **What the user sees:**\n"Transaction could not be completed.\nNo funds were moved. Please retry."

== meanwhile, in parallel — automatic failover ==
DBA_R -> DBA_R: Patroni detects primary failure,\npromotes replica within RTO 30s
note over DBA_R
  Once promoted, ACC_A's connection pool
  reconnects to new primary. CB-DB-PRIMARY
  moves to HALF_OPEN, then CLOSED after
  probe requests succeed. Next client retry
  (same idempotency key) succeeds normally.
end note

@enduml

@startuml
' Diagram 3 of 4: FAILURE SCENARIO 2 — Debit succeeds, credit fails (requires compensation)
title P2P Payment — Failure Scenario 2: Destination Shard Fails After Debit Committed

actor Client
participant "Transaction\nOrchestrator" as ORCH
participant "Payment\nProcessing Svc" as PAY
participant "Account Svc\n(Shard A - sender)" as ACC_A
participant "Account Svc\n(Shard B - receiver)" as ACC_B
database "DB Shard A" as DBA
database "DB Shard B\n(DOWN)" as DBB #FFCCCC
queue "Kafka" as KAFKA

ORCH -> PAY: process(txn)
PAY -> ACC_A: debit(account_A, amount)
ACC_A -> DBA: UPDATE ... committed
DBA --> ACC_A: success
ACC_A --> PAY: **debited — COMMITTED**

PAY -> ACC_B: credit(account_B, amount)
ACC_B -> DBB: UPDATE accounts ...
DBB --> ACC_B: **connection timeout**
ACC_B --> PAY: ERROR: SHARD_UNAVAILABLE

note over PAY, ORCH #FFCCCC
  **Compensation logic: REQUIRED.**
  The debit already committed. Money has
  left account A but never reached account B.
  Saga must run the compensating transaction
  for the completed step (credit sender back).
end note

PAY --> ORCH: step failed AFTER prior commit —\ntrigger compensation

ORCH -> ACC_A: compensate: credit(account_A, amount,\nreason=REVERSAL, ref=original_saga_id)
ACC_A -> DBA: UPDATE accounts SET available_balance += amount,\nversion = v+2 WHERE account_id=A AND version=v+1
DBA --> ACC_A: success
ACC_A --> ORCH: compensation applied

ORCH -> ORCH: UPDATE transaction SET status=REVERSED,\nfailure_reason=SHARD_UNAVAILABLE,\ncompleted_at=now()
note over ORCH
  Must complete within 30s per FR-005
  (automatic reversal SLA). Compensation
  is itself a new ledger-entry pair, not a
  deletion — audit trail (FR-004) stays
  immutable and complete.
end note

ORCH -> KAFKA: outbox: txn.reversed
ORCH --> Client: **What the user sees:**\n"Transaction failed and was automatically\nreversed. Your balance is unaffected."

@enduml

@startuml
' Diagram 4 of 4: FAILURE SCENARIO 3 — Client retry / duplicate idempotency key
title P2P Payment — Failure Scenario 3: Client Retries After Timeout (Duplicate Request)

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Transaction\nOrchestrator" as ORCH
participant "Redis\n(idempotency)" as REDIS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== original request — succeeded server-side, but response lost in transit ==
Client -> GW: POST /payments\n(Idempotency-Key: K1)
GW -> ORCH: forward
ORCH -> DB: process transaction fully\n(as in happy path)
ORCH -> REDIS: SET idempotency:K1 = COMPLETED\n{transaction_id: T1, result: {...}}
ORCH --> GW: 200 OK
GW -x Client: **response lost**\n(network timeout on client side)

== client times out, retries with SAME idempotency key ==
Client -> GW: POST /payments\n(Idempotency-Key: K1) [RETRY]
GW -> ORCH: forward
ORCH -> REDIS: GET idempotency:K1
REDIS --> ORCH: **FOUND: COMPLETED**\n{transaction_id: T1, result: {...}}

note over ORCH #CCFFCC
  **No reprocessing occurs.** The orchestrator
  detects the key already resolved and returns
  the cached original result directly. The
  debit/credit logic is never re-executed —
  this is what makes FR-002/FR-003 (idempotency
  + exactly-once business effects) hold even
  when the client cannot tell whether its first
  request succeeded.
end note

ORCH --> GW: 200 OK {transaction_id: T1, status: COMPLETED}\n(identical to original response)
GW --> Client: 200 OK — same transaction_id returned,\nno duplicate debit/credit occurred

@enduml